{"name":"Beach House","hex":"#edd481","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"beach house","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Alternative form of beachhouse."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/beach_house"}],"entries":[{"title":"Beach House","blocks":[{"text":"Beach House is an American dream pop band formed in Baltimore in 2004, consisting of current members Victoria Legrand and Alex Scally, who both met in Baltimore's indie scene, and James Barone, who joined as an official member in 2022 after touring prominently with them since 2016. The band has been regarded by journalists and critics as rejuvenating the genre of dream pop for newer generations."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/72/Beach_House_at_House_of_Blues_San_Diego_on_July_1_2012.jpg/330px-Beach_House_at_House_of_Blues_San_Diego_on_July_1_2012.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Beach_House","wikidata":"Q812842"},{"title":"Beach House (album)","blocks":[{"text":"Beach House is the debut studio album by American dream pop duo Beach House. It was released on October 3, 2006, by Carpark Records in North America, Bella Union in Europe, and Mistletone Records in Australia. After meeting each other in 2004 and later splitting from another band the following year, Daggerhearts, members Victoria Legrand and Alex Scally decided to write a set of songs together, as they wanted to form a band. They would record their debut album on a 4-track recording tape in 2005 over a two-day period in Scally's basement."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/e/ee/BeachHouse-Album.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Beach_House_(album)","wikidata":"Q3285160"},{"title":"Beach house","blocks":[{"text":"A beach house is a house on or near a beach, sometimes used as a vacation or second home for people who commute to the house on weekends or during vacation periods. Beach houses are often designed to weather the type of climate they are built in and the building materials and construction methods used in beach housing vary widely around the world.\nBeach houses require special paint to protect them from the salt water. If a property is built on sand, it needs foundation with special requirements."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/ce/Kurhaus_Zingst_2006.jpg/330px-Kurhaus_Zingst_2006.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Beach_house","wikidata":"Q3249386"},{"title":"Beach","blocks":[{"text":"A beach is a landform alongside a body of water which consists of loose particles. The particles composing a beach are typically made from rock, such as sand, gravel, shingle, pebbles, etc., or biological sources, such as mollusc shells or coralline algae. Sediments settle in different densities and structures, depending on the local wave action and weather, creating different textures, colors and gradients or layers of material."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/73/Beach_at_Fort_Lauderdale.jpg/330px-Beach_at_Fort_Lauderdale.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Beach","wikidata":"Q40080"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/af/Beach_House_at_the_High_Noon_Saloon_%282007-06-01%29.jpg/500px-Beach_House_at_the_High_Noon_Saloon_%282007-06-01%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/af/Beach_House_at_the_High_Noon_Saloon_%282007-06-01%29.jpg/500px-Beach_House_at_the_High_Noon_Saloon_%282007-06-01%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Beach House performing at the High Noon Saloon in June 2007","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ABeach_House_at_the_High_Noon_Saloon_(2007-06-01).jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/22/BeachHouse.jpg/500px-BeachHouse.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/22/BeachHouse.jpg/1280px-BeachHouse.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/22/BeachHouse.jpg/500px-BeachHouse.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Beach House performing at Siren Music Festival in July 2008","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ABeachHouse.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/28/Beach_House_Coachella_2010.jpg/500px-Beach_House_Coachella_2010.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/28/Beach_House_Coachella_2010.jpg/500px-Beach_House_Coachella_2010.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Beach House performing at Coachella 2010","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ABeach_House_Coachella_2010.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5e/Beach_House%2C_05-13-2012%2C_The_Orange_Peel%2C_Asheville%2C_NC.jpg/500px-Beach_House%2C_05-13-2012%2C_The_Orange_Peel%2C_Asheville%2C_NC.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5e/Beach_House%2C_05-13-2012%2C_The_Orange_Peel%2C_Asheville%2C_NC.jpg/1280px-Beach_House%2C_05-13-2012%2C_The_Orange_Peel%2C_Asheville%2C_NC.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5e/Beach_House%2C_05-13-2012%2C_The_Orange_Peel%2C_Asheville%2C_NC.jpg/500px-Beac